{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/797177-question-about-shadow-lords-bringer-of-lights","id":797177,"title":"Question about Shadow Lords Bringer of Lights","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T21:15:17-08:00","id":797177,"title":"Question about Shadow Lords Bringer of Lights","content":"So I've been playing since the beginning and the BoL camp is one of my question but I never really thought about it. Are the BoL known outside of the Lords? Or are they that secret the Lords keep knowing the other tribes would question the validity of a group of garou who associate with Wyrm minions? I've always played them as secret agents who avoid the spotlight but now I'm curious how you see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T23:46:51-08:00","id":797217,"title":"","content":"My impression is that they are not very known, if they are known about at all, outside of the Shadow Lord Tribe (and probably within the Tribe as well). The Uktena seem like the most likely to know anything about them, outside of the Tribe; but the Bringers of Light operate in a way that is highly antithetical to mainstream Garou instinct. They are primarily loners, they have to roll in the scent of the enemy, look the enemy, even behave like the enemy perhaps. I could see the Bringers of Light - for those who even heard the name - thinking that the camp was just an excuse to save face against Shadow Lords who have fallen.<br /> <br /> It's in the interest of the Bringers of Light to be unknown and misrepresented even, because given that any Garou can fall to the corruption of the Wyrm, if the Nation were to be aware of the Bringers and their abilities, it would undermine their efficacy as word spread or that information was taken with a fallen Garou right to the enemy's ears. As I result, I play them highly secretive, because I find it difficult to justify that they would still exist if they weren't - either that, or they are exceedingly new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:58:22-08:00","id":797330,"title":"","content":"There are probably rumors that they exist, but they're double agents. Their safety requires that they minimize contact with membrs of their own side, so the only ways you'd ever meet them are:<br /> 1) You are a Bringer of Light<br /> 2) You are their handler<br /> 3) SNAFU","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T06:47:24-08:00","id":797779,"title":"","content":"The whole point of them is that they are a secret society doing something frowned upon by the majority of the Garou society and infiltrating and disabling people and groups that need to be unaware they are targeted. So yeah. It's a Secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:35:18-08:00","id":805444,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the need to be that secretive. The revised TB fleshed them out a lot more, but before that, their write-up could be read in different ways.<br /> <br /> So, what the Light Bringers do is essentially gaining the benefits of the &quot;Immune to Wyrm Emanations&quot; Merit in-game. Sure, revised has a specific list of &quot;benefits&quot; they get but before revised, the description read just like the merit. Once this is achieved, they are basically incorruptible and therefore suited to be amongst the greatest heroes for the tribe and the garou nation. Sure, such a reputation would come at a price, especially if they needed to hide amongst Wyrm minions again at some point.<br /> <br /> That said, the camps reputation might also be overshadowed by the loss of young garou who strive to become Lightbringer, and therefore set out to be in the vicinity of corruption and fail to stay pure. I'd imagine, the success rate of garou trying to achieve a place amongst the Lightbringers is not that good. Meaning, if a pack of Lightbringers visits a Shadowlord sept, you are happy and try to marry your kin-child to them, but probably don't want your true-born-child to be too fascinated, for you don't want your child to fall to the wyrm - and failing to enter this Camp (although failing is never an option for a shadow lord) means exactly that, you become a wyrm minion. And whilst a Lighbringer would certainly be great for the reputation of the family line, a fallen Shadow Lord would be a much larger stain in the family tree, so your child better become an ordinary, sorry &quot;traditional&quot;, Shadow Lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}